From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:09:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] combase: Send back a call the message filter rejects, and
 make it again as the caller's filter says.

A call the called apartment's filter answers with SERVERCALL_RETRYLATER was
made all the same.  As Windows does it, the call now goes back unmade, and a
single-threaded apartment that has a filter asks its RetryRejectedCall whether
to give up (-1, RPC_E_CALL_REJECTED), make it again at once (under 100) or
after that many milliseconds; one without a filter gets RPC_E_CALL_REJECTED,
and the multithreaded apartment RPC_E_SERVERCALL_RETRYLATER.  The same holds
for SERVERCALL_REJECTED, the caller's filter being told which answer it got.
HandleInComingCall is told the calling thread when that is a single-threaded
apartment and 0 otherwise, instead of the called process, and
RetryRejectedCall the called apartment's thread.

Word's filter answers an in-place Excel worksheet's SetBorderSpace with
SERVERCALL_RETRYLATER while it lays out; Wine ran it inside that layout.

Measured on Windows 11 in and across processes (tools/comprobe/retrylater.c).
A request the RPC runtime sent is no longer leaked when a fault comes back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 728920b216cfc2eebef6f1437c69f3a8c5381f6e)

